WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.330
How I'm showing up every day for those around me,

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.824
that becomes my legacy.

3
00:00:04.824 --> 00:00:08.370
(bright upbeat music)

4
00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:11.520
You distill Longpath down to like a sentence.

5
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:14.270
Are you doing something for the next generation or not?

6
00:00:15.735 --> 00:00:18.356
For what we do or don't do in the next 10 to 15 years

7
00:00:18.356 --> 00:00:20.900
will have a knock on effect for hundreds

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.203
if not thousands of years.

9
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.700
Let's be honest here for a second.

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.020
Can we?

11
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:36.020
We as a global society currently face a few challenges

12
00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.420
and some of those challenges are actually existential.

13
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:42.690
They're challenges that simply cannot be solved

14
00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:44.910
with the mindset, the institutions,

15
00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:48.030
and the paradigms that are currently in place.

16
00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:51.180
Instead, these solutions require

17
00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.850
that we think beyond certain economic,

18
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:55.860
political and social constraints,

19
00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.610
and actually beyond our own individual lifespans

20
00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:04.140
to consider deeply the impact that we will have

21
00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.140
on many generations into the future.

22
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.530
They require an applied mindset that today's guest,

23
00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:13.290
Ari Wallach calls Longpath,

24
00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:15.720
which is a way of being,

25
00:01:15.720 --> 00:01:19.860
it's a verb that cultivates future conscious thinking

26
00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:23.940
and behavior to build more hopeful visions for the future,

27
00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:26.100
turn those visions into action,

28
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:27.360
and while we're at it,

29
00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.170
build more meaning into our lives and our legacies.

30
00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.080
Ari is a futurist although he hates that term,

31
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:37.170
he is a social system strategist.

32
00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:40.470
He's also the author of a brand new book out this week

33
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.740
aptly-titled you might have guessed it "Longpath",

34
00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.040
which extends a discussion that he began

35
00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.490
with his 2017 Ted Talk entitled

36
00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:55.323
Short-Termism is Killing Us: It's Time for Longpath.

37
00:01:55.323 --> 00:01:59.130
This conversation asks a very simple question,

38
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:04.020
how do we become great ancestors to our future descendants?

39
00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:06.480
And the answer lies in upending

40
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.090
our traditional thinking around the future.

41
00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.520
It entails developing something called

42
00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.920
transgenerational empathy,

43
00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.170
and it involves orienting your life around

44
00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:21.090
this idea of telos, a life quest that is bigger than you

45
00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.000
that will help you make peace with death

46
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:27.600
and guard your lived experience with greater meaning,

47
00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.243
greater purpose, and greater fulfillment.

48
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:32.310
I really enjoy talking to Ari.

49
00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:36.240
I think this one just might leave you reevaluating your path

50
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.000
and your priorities in a positive way.

51
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.690
