give us $100 million and we're gonna put your name

2064
01:23:31.080 --> 01:23:32.190
on the side of this building.

2065
01:23:32.190 --> 01:23:34.740
You will live forever in this building.

2066
01:23:34.740 --> 01:23:38.580
And it's a great way to raise huge gifts

2067
01:23:38.580 --> 01:23:41.091
is to connect someone's legacy with a...

2068
01:23:41.091 --> 01:23:42.780
They always do it in marble.

2069
01:23:42.780 --> 01:23:43.620
I always find it interesting,

2070
01:23:43.620 --> 01:23:45.090
the names on the sides of buildings

2071
01:23:45.090 --> 01:23:47.010
are the same kind of marble they use for tombstones.

2072
01:23:47.010 --> 01:23:48.090
I don't know like it's it.

2073
01:23:48.090 --> 01:23:48.923
It's always amazing that we do that.

2074
01:23:48.923 --> 01:23:50.190
I never thought of that.

2075
01:23:50.190 --> 01:23:52.320
And look, I'm not gonna have hundreds of millions

2076
01:23:52.320 --> 01:23:53.670
of dollars to put my name on the side of the building.

2077
01:23:53.670 --> 01:23:58.370
But I have three kids, a wife aforementioned Ozzie,

2078
01:23:58.370 --> 01:24:00.960
and a whole bunch of people that I interact with,

2079
01:24:00.960 --> 01:24:02.610
thousands of people that I interact with.

2080
01:24:02.610 --> 01:24:05.640
So how I am going to build a legacy

2081
01:24:05.640 --> 01:24:09.720
of making tomorrow better is how I am going to interact

2082
01:24:09.720 --> 01:24:14.430
with those people on a moment by moment, day-to-day basis.

2083
01:24:14.430 --> 01:24:15.840
That becomes my legacy.

2084
01:24:15.840 --> 01:24:18.150
Look, like I said, I have three kids.

2085
01:24:18.150 --> 01:24:22.440
So based on some math, two, 300 years from now,

2086
01:24:22.440 --> 01:24:25.530
I'm gonna have eight to 9,000 descendants

2087
01:24:25.530 --> 01:24:27.483
assuming certain things happen.

2088
01:24:28.920 --> 01:24:29.910
That's a lot of people.

2089
01:24:29.910 --> 01:24:31.470
Now sometimes when people say that,

2090
01:24:31.470 --> 01:24:32.400
they're like, oh, it's genetic.

2091
01:24:32.400 --> 01:24:33.233
I'm not talking about genetic,

2092
01:24:33.233 --> 01:24:35.040
I'm talking about ways of being.

2093
01:24:35.040 --> 01:24:37.410
So I said earlier, in my family we grew up

2094
01:24:37.410 --> 01:24:39.990
having dinner together and we talked about things.

2095
01:24:39.990 --> 01:24:41.820
We're doing the same thing in my family.

2096
01:24:41.820 --> 01:24:43.770
The way I interact with my colleagues,

2097
01:24:43.770 --> 01:24:44.850
with the humans that I know,

2098
01:24:44.850 --> 01:24:46.950
the way I hopefully interact with Rich Roll,

2099
01:24:46.950 --> 01:24:49.800
what that ends up doing is creating a kind of,

2100
01:24:49.800 --> 01:24:54.690
and this is complexity theory or chaos theory, many ways,

2101
01:24:54.690 --> 01:24:56.730
reverberations that go throughout time,

2102
01:24:56.730 --> 01:24:58.260
that becomes my legacy,

2103
01:24:58.260 --> 01:25:00.240
not my name on the side of a building.

2104
01:25:00.240 --> 01:25:01.440
So that's a Longpath is,

2105
01:25:01.440 --> 01:25:03.600
it becomes a kind of immortality project.

2106
01:25:03.600 --> 01:25:05.340
Your name's not connected to it,

2107
01:25:05.340 --> 01:25:08.460
but your character and your way of being in the world is,

2108
01:25:08.460 --> 01:25:12.300
and if we want to kind of set up these hundreds of billions,

2109
01:25:12.300 --> 01:25:14.400
if not trillions of humans to come,

2110
01:25:14.400 --> 01:25:15.840
we have to start acting like that.

2111
01:25:15.840 --> 01:25:16.673
Yeah.

2112
01:25:16.673 --> 01:25:19.320
What I love about that is it really recalibrates

2113
01:25:19.320 --> 01:25:21.570
our relationship with this idea of legacy.

2114
01:25:21.570 --> 01:25:23.670
It's a very expansive definition.

2115
01:25:23.670 --> 01:25:25.380
I mean, traditionally we think of legacy

2116
01:25:25.380 --> 01:25:28.980
as what are they gonna say about me when I die,

2117
01:25:28.980 --> 01:25:30.270
and how much money did I have,

2118
01:25:30.270 --> 01:25:31.449
and what are the accomplishments

2119
01:25:31.449 --> 01:25:33.270
that are gonna show up in my obid

2120
01:25:33.270 --> 01:25:36.180
or is my name gonna be on a building

2121
01:25:36.180 --> 01:25:38.220
for the very few people.

2122
01:25:38.220 --> 01:25:40.930
But really we all have a legacy

2123
01:25:41.790 --> 01:25:44.972
and that is completely detached from accomplishments

2124
01:25:44.972 --> 01:25:48.480
or your bank account, or social approval.

2125
01:25:48.480 --> 01:25:51.570
Because in every interaction that we have throughout the day

2126
01:25:51.570 --> 01:25:53.730
has an impact and there are ripple effects

2127
01:25:53.730 --> 01:25:54.563
that go from that.

2128
01:25:54.563 --> 01:25:58.560
So to think about legacy not as we're nearing the end

2129
01:25:58.560 --> 01:25:59.940
of our professional lives,

2130
01:25:59.940 --> 01:26:04.230
but to really embody or to be contemplating legacy,

2131
01:26:04.230 --> 01:26:05.550
even as a young person,

2132
01:26:05.550 --> 01:26:07.590
I think is a really powerful lever

2133
01:26:07.590 --> 01:26:10.350
for how you think about constructing your life

2134
01:26:10.350 --> 01:26:15.224
and the avenues for your energy and attention.

2135
01:26:15.224 --> 01:26:18.870
Where you put your energy and attention

2136
01:26:18.870 --> 01:26:22.440
and how you behave with yourself and with others

2137
01:26:22.440 --> 01:26:25.020
are heirlooms in the making.

2138
01:26:25.020 --> 01:26:27.930
We often think about heirlooms as furniture or as jewelry,

2139
01:26:27.930 --> 01:26:29.844
but there's also emotional heirlooms.

2140
01:26:29.844 --> 01:26:32.280
There's these ways of being.

2141
01:26:32.280 --> 01:26:35.940
Look, and I've seen how those can be bad.

2142
01:26:35.940 --> 01:26:39.540
If we look at a lot of kind of consistent,

2143
01:26:39.540 --> 01:26:41.910
terrible systemic traumas that are happening,

2144
01:26:41.910 --> 01:26:44.490
domestic abuse at a whole bunch of other things,

2145
01:26:44.490 --> 01:26:45.750
all the experts that I've talked to say,

2146
01:26:45.750 --> 01:26:49.350
well, anyone who is doing that right now

2147
01:26:49.350 --> 01:26:51.327
that happened to them, that happened to them.

2148
01:26:51.327 --> 01:26:54.513
And that's at the acute horrific scale.

2149
01:26:55.890 --> 01:26:57.810
Now we can flip that and say, well, what does

2150
01:26:57.810 --> 01:27:00.150
that look like on the opposite side?

2151
01:27:00.150 --> 01:27:04.740
So if we start, I was in the room, a very large room,

2152
01:27:04.740 --> 01:27:09.030
with the Dalai Lama once and you can feel that energy.

2153
01:27:09.030 --> 01:27:12.450
And I read about Mother Teresa, and Krishnamurti,

2154
01:27:12.450 --> 01:27:14.370
and Gandhi and the brilliance of Einstein

2155
01:27:14.370 --> 01:27:15.720
and all these folks.

2156
01:27:15.720 --> 01:27:20.160
And from things that I've read,

2157
01:27:20.160 --> 01:27:23.760
the legacies are about how they were

2158
01:27:23.760 --> 01:27:25.740
in the moment with folks.

2159
01:27:25.740 --> 01:27:29.490
So now think about, yes, his holiness of Dalai Lama

2160
01:27:29.490 --> 01:27:30.930
is an en enlightened one.

2161
01:27:30.930 --> 01:27:34.020
But what you can say is very clearly

2162
01:27:34.020 --> 01:27:36.240
he has chosen and made a decision

2163
01:27:36.240 --> 01:27:39.600
to be love constantly, consistently.

2164
01:27:39.600 --> 01:27:43.260
So if we think about how we want other future generations

2165
01:27:43.260 --> 01:27:44.520
to live and exist,

2166
01:27:44.520 --> 01:27:47.400
not in a kind of mechanistic society

2167
01:27:47.400 --> 01:27:50.130
where we see each other in an instrumental way,

2168
01:27:50.130 --> 01:27:52.590
these kind of industrial enlightenment ways,

2169
01:27:52.590 --> 01:27:54.630
but we wanna see something very different.

2170
01:27:54.630 --> 01:27:55.980
How do we choose that?

2171
01:27:55.980 --> 01:27:58.080
Because when I talk about in the book is the project.

2172
01:27:58.080 --> 01:27:59.850
When I talk about this larger telos,

2173
01:27:59.850 --> 01:28:01.650
I talk about human flourishing.

2174
01:28:01.650 --> 01:28:05.067
Moving from, I need stuff to a sense of being

2175
01:28:05.067 --> 01:28:06.930
and a sense of caring.

2176
01:28:06.930 --> 01:28:09.818
But those are the words that I use,

2177
01:28:09.818 --> 01:28:12.510
and I do use love, but that's really what it is.

2178
01:28:12.510 --> 01:28:13.920
That's what we wanna be, that's what we wanna...

2179
01:28:13.920 --> 01:28:16.020
Now, it's very difficult to do.

2180
01:28:16.020 --> 01:28:16.853
I write about in the book,

2181
01:28:16.853 --> 01:28:18.237
I get these arguments with my wife and my kids

2182
01:28:18.237 --> 01:28:19.298
and all these things.

2183
01:28:19.298 --> 01:28:22.636
It's kind of like, you see people with these wristbands,

2184
01:28:22.636 --> 01:28:23.910
like what would Jesus do?

2185
01:28:23.910 --> 01:28:25.393
And it's like, well, what would the Dalai Lama do?

2186
01:28:25.393 --> 01:28:27.120
What would the Dalai Lama do?

2187
01:28:27.120 --> 01:28:29.040
How would the Dalai Lama reacting be?

2188
01:28:29.040 --> 01:28:30.030
That's really what you wanna do,

2189
01:28:30.030 --> 01:28:32.280
because as you start doing that,

2190
01:28:32.280 --> 01:28:34.200
and we know the science behind this.

2191
01:28:34.200 --> 01:28:37.080
We know about adrenaline and cortisol, and dopamine.

2192
01:28:37.080 --> 01:28:39.960
And if we wanna start kind of tweaking those,

2193
01:28:39.960 --> 01:28:41.880
'cause on the one hand we have Silicon Valley

2194
01:28:41.880 --> 01:28:43.590
totally tweaking the levers, right?

2195
01:28:43.590 --> 01:28:45.720
Just like ramping up the dopamine and cortisol

2196
01:28:45.720 --> 01:28:47.250
and shock da, da.

2197
01:28:47.250 --> 01:28:48.960
So we're the change.

2198
01:28:48.960 --> 01:28:50.250
The way we interact with others,

2199
01:28:50.250 --> 01:28:51.450
it's gonna start shaping the future.

2200
01:28:51.450 --> 01:28:52.860
We're the firewall.

2201
01:28:52.860 --> 01:28:56.130
Our moment to moment actions are the firewall

2202
01:28:56.130 --> 01:28:59.640
from having a world dissolve into one of kind of anger

2203
01:28:59.640 --> 01:29:01.440
and bitterness as opposed to kind of one

2204
01:29:01.440 --> 01:29:03.198
of human flourishing in love.

2205
01:29:03.198 --> 01:29:06.150
So with that though, this idea of telos

2206
01:29:06.150 --> 01:29:10.500
and embodying a certain type of sensibility

2207
01:29:10.500 --> 01:29:13.041
and orienting your life around something bigger

2208
01:29:13.041 --> 01:29:17.320
than yourself, you still have to build into that

2209
01:29:18.540 --> 01:29:21.810
this notion of what your horizon looks like, right?

2210
01:29:21.810 --> 01:29:23.820
You call it like your Ithaca.

2211
01:29:23.820 --> 01:29:26.070
Like what is your Ithaca?

2212
01:29:26.070 --> 01:29:29.370
Which begs the question of whether we as a society

2213
01:29:29.370 --> 01:29:32.940
or humanity in general has ever had an Ithaca.

2214
01:29:32.940 --> 01:29:34.593
So explain that concept.

2215
01:29:36.044 --> 01:29:38.740
So this goes back to my time at UC Berkeley

2216
01:29:39.600 --> 01:29:41.790
when I was writing my honors thesis

2217
01:29:41.790 --> 01:29:43.800
I called it Ithaca lost.

2218
01:29:43.800 --> 01:29:46.530
And it was kind of this idea that we had lost

2219
01:29:46.530 --> 01:29:48.150
as a society our Ithaca.

2220
01:29:48.150 --> 01:29:49.620
So let's go back.

2221
01:29:49.620 --> 01:29:50.520
In the Odyssey or thesis--

2222
01:29:50.520 --> 01:29:51.359
You have to go way back.

2223
01:29:51.359 --> 01:29:52.333
Let's go way, way back.

2224
01:29:52.333 --> 01:29:56.070
Odyssey is this maroon and he wants to get back to Ithaca,

2225
01:29:56.070 --> 01:29:57.780
he wants to get to his love, his Penelope,

2226
01:29:57.780 --> 01:29:58.887
but it's really Ithaca.

2227
01:29:58.887 --> 01:30:01.253
But we could argue whether it was Penelope or Ithaca

2228
01:30:01.253 --> 01:30:03.960
back to the ruling power, which one it was.

2229
01:30:03.960 --> 01:30:05.760
But let's just say it was a kind of Ithaca,

2230
01:30:05.760 --> 01:30:08.610
Penelope combination, but we'll stick with Ithaca right now.

2231
01:30:08.610 --> 01:30:09.443
And he wanted to get back.

2232
01:30:09.443 --> 01:30:10.680
So he went through all these different things,

2233
01:30:10.680 --> 01:30:12.960
and the monsters, and the sirens, and all these things.

2234
01:30:12.960 --> 01:30:14.730
But it was his goal was to kind of,

2235
01:30:14.730 --> 01:30:17.760
his ultimate aim was to return back there.

2236
01:30:17.760 --> 01:30:21.240
And so what telo says is would and yes,

2237
01:30:21.240 --> 01:30:23.550
Ithaca in a certain sense was a place,

2238
01:30:23.550 --> 01:30:26.370
but it's really a kind of state of being back to home,

2239
01:30:26.370 --> 01:30:27.480
back to where you belong,

2240
01:30:27.480 --> 01:30:30.093
back to something bigger than yourself.

2241
01:30:31.410 --> 01:30:32.633
And what I write about in the book is,

2242
01:30:32.633 --> 01:30:34.770
and I'm really questioning,

2243
01:30:34.770 --> 01:30:36.840
like do we have an Ithaca right now?

2244
01:30:36.840 --> 01:30:39.960
I know we had an American dream like a picket fence

2245
01:30:39.960 --> 01:30:41.070
and I know there's different...

2246
01:30:41.070 --> 01:30:44.040
And I know it's also coming from Western privilege

2247
01:30:44.040 --> 01:30:46.350
because when I walk out of here I'll be able

2248
01:30:46.350 --> 01:30:48.300
to get into my car and go buy food.

2249
01:30:48.300 --> 01:30:50.880
So on a Maslowian sense,

2250
01:30:50.880 --> 01:30:54.060
kind of the first two steps on that pyramid to say

2251
01:30:54.060 --> 01:30:56.310
to even have this conversation of a larger Ithaca

2252
01:30:56.310 --> 01:30:58.200
for homo sapiens, first and foremost,

2253
01:30:58.200 --> 01:30:59.760
we have to bring everyone up to a certain level.

2254
01:30:59.760 --> 01:31:00.593
Let's start there.

2255
01:31:00.593 --> 01:31:01.620
This is kind of the Bucky thing

2256
01:31:01.620 --> 01:31:03.240
that you talked about earlier.

2257
01:31:03.240 --> 01:31:04.347
But then within that,

2258
01:31:04.347 --> 01:31:07.380
and I would argue that without this larger Ithaca,

2259
01:31:07.380 --> 01:31:09.390
we won't even be able to get to that.

2260
01:31:09.390 --> 01:31:11.700
Where is it that we wanna get to

2261
01:31:11.700 --> 01:31:14.010
as a species on planet earth?

2262
01:31:14.010 --> 01:31:16.531
'Cause right now, look, this is one of the things...

2263
01:31:16.531 --> 01:31:19.470
So the treaty of west Follia that ended the 100 years war,

2264
01:31:19.470 --> 01:31:22.380
created the nation state about 400 years old.

2265
01:31:22.380 --> 01:31:24.960
So that's another thing that we kind of dissolved

2266
01:31:24.960 --> 01:31:25.920
at the end of this intertidals,

2267
01:31:25.920 --> 01:31:28.120
even the idea of a nation state and borders.

2268
01:31:29.520 --> 01:31:31.151
So putting the nation state aside

2269
01:31:31.151 --> 01:31:34.800
and just saying as a species on the planet

2270
01:31:34.800 --> 01:31:36.600
regardless of whether or not there's kind of nation states

2271
01:31:36.600 --> 01:31:39.870
involved in this part of the conversation,

2272
01:31:39.870 --> 01:31:42.960
what do we want it to look like two, 3000 years from now?

2273
01:31:42.960 --> 01:31:44.510
Because like, here's the thing.

2274
01:31:46.284 --> 01:31:50.850
So I've seen a bunch of movies from like Roman gladiators

2275
01:31:50.850 --> 01:31:52.410
and I went to go visit the Coliseum once

2276
01:31:52.410 --> 01:31:53.400
with my family.

2277
01:31:53.400 --> 01:31:56.550
And it was amazing and it seemed like so long ago.

2278
01:31:56.550 --> 01:32:00.360
But here's the thing, the year 4,020 A.D,

2279
01:32:00.360 --> 01:32:01.650
which seems like so...

2280
01:32:01.650 --> 01:32:03.570
Like think about most of the science fiction we see

2281
01:32:03.570 --> 01:32:05.880
none of it goes out to the year 4,000.

2282
01:32:05.880 --> 01:32:09.030
But the year 4,020 A.D,

2283
01:32:09.030 --> 01:32:11.640
we're closer to that than we are to the Coliseum

2284
01:32:11.640 --> 01:32:13.054
in Roman times.

2285
01:32:13.054 --> 01:32:14.430
So even though what I'm,

2286
01:32:14.430 --> 01:32:16.290
sounds like what I'm talking about is really out there.

2287
01:32:16.290 --> 01:32:17.760
It really isn't.

2288
01:32:17.760 --> 01:32:19.200
We're literally kind of flipping

2289
01:32:19.200 --> 01:32:20.460
the lever over on history.

2290
01:32:20.460 --> 01:32:22.590
So if we want to get to that,

2291
01:32:22.590 --> 01:32:25.020
we have to have a real honest conversation about where it is

2292
01:32:25.020 --> 01:32:26.100
that we want to go to,

2293
01:32:26.100 --> 01:32:27.750
not just cause we need to have the conversation,

2294
01:32:27.750 --> 01:32:29.310
but because what I alluded to earlier

2295
01:32:29.310 --> 01:32:31.230
that without having that conversation,

2296
01:32:31.230 --> 01:32:33.153
that emotional connection of what

2297
01:32:33.153 --> 01:32:35.160
that protopia could look like.

2298
01:32:35.160 --> 01:32:37.063
So it's not dystopia, it's not utopia,

2299
01:32:37.063 --> 01:32:40.483
which means no place, but protopia,

2300
01:32:40.483 --> 01:32:41.970
a term Kevin Kelly came up with,

2301
01:32:41.970 --> 01:32:44.070
which is a tomorrow better than today.

2302
01:32:44.070 --> 01:32:49.070
If we want these protopia in 4,020 A.D if not sooner,

2303
01:32:49.470 --> 01:32:52.560
my argument is without that vision of what that looks like,

2304
01:32:52.560 --> 01:32:54.630
what that land of milk and honey looks like.

2305
01:32:54.630 --> 01:32:57.643
Remember, well, I won't say we are.

2306
01:32:57.643 --> 01:32:59.040
I won't bring you into my story.

2307
01:32:59.040 --> 01:33:01.800
But when we, the Hebrews were slaves and we left Egypt

2308
01:33:01.800 --> 01:33:03.510
and we didn't wanna go further

2309
01:33:03.510 --> 01:33:05.730
or say no, Moses, we can't go further,

2310
01:33:05.730 --> 01:33:06.563
he came back and said,

2311
01:33:06.563 --> 01:33:08.700
no, no, there's a land of milk and honey.

2312
01:33:08.700 --> 01:33:11.580
Here's a vision of a place, a way of being.

2313
01:33:11.580 --> 01:33:13.950
And I know that's nothing metaphor,

2314
01:33:13.950 --> 01:33:15.930
but man, there was some good marketing in that.

2315
01:33:15.930 --> 01:33:18.180
Because without that land of milk and honey,

